    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Prioritized Experience Replay (PER) - Empirische Untersuchung\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Umfassende Analyse und Visualisierung\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Dieses Notebook führt eine detaillierte empirische Analyse von Prioritized Experience Replay (PER) durch und vergleicht es mit klassischem Uniform Replay.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Konzeptionelle Grundlagen von PER\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.1 Was ist Prioritized Experience Replay?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Prioritized Experience Replay (PER)** ist eine Optimierungsmethode für Deep Reinforcement Learning, die die Effizienz des Trainings durch intelligente Auswahl von Trainingsdaten erhöht.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Kernidee:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Nicht alle Erfahrungen sind gleich wertvoll**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Erfahrungen mit hohem TD-Error (Temporal Difference Error) sind für das Lernen wichtiger\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Diese sollten häufiger als Trainingsmaterial verwendet werden\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Mathematisches Konzept:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$P(i) = \\\\frac{p_i^{\\\\alpha}}{\\\\sum_k p_k^{\\\\alpha}}$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wobei:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- $p_i$ = Priorität der Erfahrung $i$ (basierend auf TD-Error)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- $\\\\alpha$ = Hyperparameter (0 = Uniform Replay, 1 = Pure Prioritization)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.2 Wie funktioniert der Replay Buffer?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Uniform Replay Buffer:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Speichern**: Alle Transitions werden in einer FIFO-Queue (First-In-First-Out) gespeichert\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Sampling**: Zufälliges Sampling mit gleichmäßiger Wahrscheinlichkeit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Update**: Priorities sind immer gleich\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Buffer: [Trans1, Trans2, Trans3, Trans4, Trans5, ...]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                ↓ random.sample()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        [Trans4, Trans1, Trans3]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        Wahrscheinlichkeit: P = 1/N für jede\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Prioritized Replay Buffer:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Speichern**: Transitions mit Priorität (based on TD-Error) speichern\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Datenstruktur**: SumTree für effiziente Prioritäts-Abfragen\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Sampling**: Probabilistisches Sampling basierend auf Prioritäten\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **Update**: Nach jedem Training: neue TD-Error → neue Prioritäten\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Buffer mit Prioritäten: \\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Trans1: p=0.1 (TD-Error: klein)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Trans2: p=0.8 (TD-Error: groß) ← häufiger sampelt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Trans3: p=0.5 (TD-Error: mittel)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Trans4: p=0.2 (TD-Error: klein)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"Wahrscheinlichkeit: P(i) = p_i / (p1 + p2 + p3 + p4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.3 Vorteile von PER\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Vorteil | Erklärung |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|----------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Schnelleres Lernen** | Schwierige Samples werden häufiger trainiert |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Bessere Ressourcen-Nutzung** | Weniger \\\"Verschwendung\\\" auf einfache Samples |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Robusteres Training** | Fokus auf wichtige Transitions verhindert Instabilität |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Bessere Konvergenz** | Schnellere und stabilere Konvergenz zu besseren Policies |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### 1.4 Nachteile und Herausforderungen\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Nachteil | Erklärung |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|----------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Hinzufügen von Bias** | Bevorzugung hoher TD-Errors kann zu Overfitting führen |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Komplexität** | SumTree-Struktur schwieriger zu implementieren |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Recency-Bias** | Könnten neue, schwierige Samples überrepräsentiert sein |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Höherer Speicher-Overhead** | Prioritäten für alle Samples speichern |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **Importance-Sampling Weights** | Notwendig zur Bias-Korrektur (kompliziert) |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### 1.5 Wann hilft PER besonders?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"✅ **PER ist besonders nützlich bei:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Umgebungen mit **sparse rewards** (schwer, überhaupt Reward zu bekommen)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Komplexen Umgebungen**, wo eine kleine Menge von Samples extrem wichtig ist\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Sample-Effizienz ist kritisch** (z.B. Robotik mit hohen Kosten)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Langzeitabhängigkeiten** in der Policy wichtig sind\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"✗ **PER ist weniger hilfreich bei:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Einfachen Environments** (kurze Episodes, klare Rewards)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Großen Buffers** (uniform sampling schon gut genug)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Online-Learning** mit kontinuierlichen Updates\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.6 Wann kann PER instabil werden?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"⚠️ **Instabilitäts-Quellen bei PER:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Zu hohe Prioritäten-Differenzen**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Wenn einige Samples viel häufiger als andere gewählt werden\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Lösung: Alpha-Hyperparameter reduzieren (mehr Uniform)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Initialiale TD-Error-Überschätzung**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Neue Samples bekommen max_priority, werden zu oft sampelt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Lösung: max_priority decay oder epsilon-add für neue Samples\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Veraltete Prioritäten**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - TD-Error ändert sich, Prioritäten folgen nicht schnell genug\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Lösung: Häufigere Prioritäts-Updates\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **Importance-Sampling-Fehler**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Wenn Importance-Sampling Weights nicht richtig korrigiert\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Kann zu extrem großen oder kleinen Gradienten führen\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"5. **Distribution Shift**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Policy ändert sich, alte Priorities passen nicht mehr\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Buffer enthält veraltete Erfahrungen mit falschen Priorities\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Setup\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import seaborn as sns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from scipy import stats\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import json\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pathlib import Path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import warnings\\n\",\n",
    "    \"warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set Style\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.set_style(\\\"whitegrid\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.set_palette(\\\"husl\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (14, 7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 11\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Daten laden\\n\",\n",
    "    \"output_dir = Path('/home/isc-den/cas-artificial-intelligence/11_dqn_extensions')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Wenn results_summary.json existiert, laden\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results_file = output_dir / 'results_summary.json'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if results_file.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    with open(results_file, 'r') as f:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        results = json.load(f)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"✓ Trainingsergebnisse geladen\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"⚠ results_summary.json nicht gefunden. Werden später laden.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Experimentelles Setup\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 2.1 Experimentelle Konfiguration\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Environment:** LunarLander-v3\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Klassisches Deep RL Problem\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Kontinuierliche Observationen (8-dimensional)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Diskrete Aktionen (4 Möglichkeiten)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Episodic Task (Terminal State)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Trainings-Parameter:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Total Steps: 300,000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Replay Buffer Size: 200,000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Batch Size: 256\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Learning Rate: 0.002\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Gamma (Discount): 0.99\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Target Update: Every 2,000 steps (with Soft Update τ=0.005)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**PER-spezifische Parameter:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Alpha (Prioritization Strength): 0.6\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Beta (Importance-Sampling Exponent): 0.4 → 1.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Epsilon (Minimum Priority): 1e-6\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Vergleich:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Baseline**: Uniform Replay (klassischer DQN)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Experimental**: Prioritized Experience Replay (PER)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3. Trainings-Ergebnisse Analyse\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Visualisierung 1: Evaluation Return Vergleich\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(15, 7))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if 'uniform' in results and 'per' in results:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    uniform_means = np.array(results['uniform']['eval_means'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    uniform_stds = np.array(results['uniform']['eval_stds'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    uniform_steps = np.array(results['uniform']['eval_steps']) / 1000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    per_means = np.array(results['per']['eval_means'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    per_stds = np.array(results['per']['eval_stds'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    per_steps = np.array(results['per']['eval_steps']) / 1000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Plot\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(uniform_steps, uniform_means, 'o-', linewidth=3, markersize=8, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label='Uniform Replay (Baseline)', color='#1f77b4', alpha=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.fill_between(uniform_steps, uniform_means - uniform_stds, uniform_means + uniform_stds, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"                     alpha=0.2, color='#1f77b4')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(per_steps, per_means, 's-', linewidth=3, markersize=8,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label='Prioritized Experience Replay (PER)', color='#ff7f0e', alpha=0.9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.fill_between(per_steps, per_means - per_stds, per_means + per_stds,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                     alpha=0.2, color='#ff7f0e')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_xlabel('Training Steps (thousands)', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_ylabel('Evaluation Return', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title('Performance Comparison: Uniform Replay vs. PER\\\\n(LunarLander-v3, 300k steps)', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"                fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.legend(fontsize=12, loc='lower right', framealpha=0.95)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, linestyle='--')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Annotationen\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.axhline(y=200, color='green', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, alpha=0.5, label='Target Return (200)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.savefig(output_dir / 'viz_01_eval_return.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"✓ Saved: viz_01_eval_return.png\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Visualisierung 2: Detaillierter Vergleich\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(16, 12))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if 'uniform' in results and 'per' in results:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Subplot 1: Final Performance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax = axes[0, 0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    methods = ['Uniform Replay', 'PER']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    final_returns = [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        results['uniform']['eval_means'][-1],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        results['per']['eval_means'][-1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    colors = ['#1f77b4', '#ff7f0e']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    bars = ax.bar(methods, final_returns, color=colors, alpha=0.8, edgecolor='black', linewidth=2.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for bar, val in zip(bars, final_returns):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        height = bar.get_height()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"               f'{val:.1f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_ylabel('Final Return', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title('Final Performance', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_ylim([0, max(final_returns) * 1.15])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Subplot 2: Max Performance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax = axes[0, 1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    max_returns = [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        max(results['uniform']['eval_means']),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        max(results['per']['eval_means'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    bars = ax.bar(methods, max_returns, color=colors, alpha=0.8, edgecolor='black', linewidth=2.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for bar, val in zip(bars, max_returns):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        height = bar.get_height()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"               f'{val:.1f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_ylabel('Maximum Return', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title('Best Performance During Training', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_ylim([0, max(max_returns) * 1.15])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Subplot 3: Convergence Speed (Steps to reach 200)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax = axes[1, 0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    threshold = 200\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    convergence_steps = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for res_name in ['uniform', 'per']:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        means = np.array(results[res_name]['eval_means'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        steps = np.array(results[res_name]['eval_steps'])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        converged_idx = np.where(means >= threshold)[0]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if len(converged_idx) > 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            convergence_steps.append(steps[converged_idx[0]] / 1000)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            convergence_steps.append(300)  # max steps\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    bars = ax.bar(methods, convergence_steps, color=colors, alpha=0.8, edgecolor='black', linewidth=2.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for bar, val in zip(bars, convergence_steps):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        height = bar.get_height()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"               f'{val:.1f}k', ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_ylabel('Training Steps (thousands)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(f'Convergence Speed (Target Return: {threshold})', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.axhline(y=300, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Subplot 4: Improvement Metrics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax = axes[1, 1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.axis('off')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Calculate metrics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    improvement = results['per']['eval_means'][-1] - results['uniform']['eval_means'][-1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    improvement_pct = (improvement / abs(results['uniform']['eval_means'][-1])) * 100\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    metrics_text = f\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"VERBESSERUNG DURCH PER\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Final Return Difference:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Uniform: {results['uniform']['eval_means'][-1]:.2f}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  PER:     {results['per']['eval_means'][-1]:.2f}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Δ:       {improvement:+.2f} ({improvement_pct:+.1f}%)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Statistical Significance:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  p-value: {results.get('p_value', 'N/A')}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Max Return Improvement:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Uniform: {max(results['uniform']['eval_means']):.2f}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  PER:     {max(results['per']['eval_means']):.2f}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sample Efficiency (Convergence):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  Uniform: {convergence_steps[0]:.1f}k steps\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  PER:     {convergence_steps[1]:.1f}k steps\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.text(0.05, 0.95, metrics_text, transform=ax.transAxes,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"           fontsize=11, verticalalignment='top', fontfamily='monospace',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"           bbox=dict(boxstyle='round', facecolor='wheat', alpha=0.8, pad=1))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.suptitle('Detailed Performance Metrics: Uniform Replay vs. PER', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"                fontsize=15, fontweight='bold', y=0.995)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.savefig(output_dir / 'viz_02_detailed_comparison.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"✓ Saved: viz_02_detailed_comparison.png\\\")\\n\",\n",
